.TH DLIST_ADD_AFTER 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
dlist_add_after \- Add a node after another node in a doubly linked list

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/dlist.h>

.IB void
.IB dlist_add_after(dlist* l, node* p, node* after);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBdlist_add_after\fR function adds a new node \fIp\fR after another node \fBafter\fR in a doubly linked list \fBl\fR. If \fBafter\fR is the tail of the list, the function calls \fBdlist_push\fR to add the node at the end of the list.

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.IB l
The doubly linked list to which the node will be added.
.TP
.IB p
The new node to be added.
.TP
.IB after
The node after which the new node will be added.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The function does not return a value.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBdlist_add_after\fR function:

.nf
#include <lib/dlist.h>

int main() {
    dlist l;
    dlist_init(&l);

    node node1, node2, node3;
    dlist_node_init(&node1);
    dlist_node_init(&node2);
    dlist_node_init(&node3);

    dlist_push(&l, &node1);
    dlist_push(&l, &node2);

    dlist_add_after(&l, &node3, &node1); // Add node3 after node1

    return 0;
}
.nef